# Two Different Radar Alternatives
Assume two radar candidates:
Radar A → 10 Hz
Radar B → 20 Hz

so the sampling frequency is:
sampling frequency: saniyede kac ölcüm yaptigi
Sampling period: iki ölcüm arasinda gecen süre
Processing time: softwarein bir ölcümü islemek icin harcadigi süre
10 Hz → one measurement every 100 ms
20 Hz → one measurement every 50 ms

However: 20 Hz is not automatically better than 10 Hz.
First, we need to understand the system requirements. Suppose the requirement is:
Radar update rate shall be ≥ 10 Hz.
So both radar options satisfies the requirements.
The decision must therefore consider additional criteria:
detection range
Field of View
accuracy
latency
interface compatibility
environmental conditions
processing requirements
power consumption
cost

Do not start with: "20 Hz is better."
Start with: "What does my system require?"
Then evaluate candidate solutions against those requirements.

